meta {
  name: POST negative quantity — 400 immediate reject
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/odata/v4/orders/Orders
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "customerId": "CUST-001",
    "quantity": -5,
    "region": "EMEA"
  }
}

docs {
  ## req.reject demo — hard stop on invalid data

  Send a POST with quantity -5.

  The before handler:
  1. Checks req.data.quantity <= 0 — true, -5 is negative
  2. Calls req.reject(400, 'Quantity must be a positive number')
  3. The handler stops immediately — no code after req.reject runs
  4. CAP rolls back the transaction — nothing is written

  Expected: 400 Bad Request — "Quantity must be a positive number"
  Run the next request (valid order) to confirm nothing was written for this one —
  no row with quantity -5 will ever show up in a GET.
}
